<Project>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Dev override (docs/architecture/repositories.md, ago-root): set the AgoFaqDevOverride environment
    variable to swap Ago.Platform.* PackageReferences for ProjectReferences into a sibling
    ../ago-platform checkout, for a change that spans this repository and the platform.

      AgoFaqDevOverride=true dotnet build            (bash)
      $env:AgoFaqDevOverride = 'true'; dotnet build  (PowerShell)

    Named for the repository that honours it, not for what it points at - the same "one name per
    repository" call ago-calendar's own AgoCalendarDevOverride and ago-chat's own
    AgoPlatformDevOverride already made: a single shared variable would retarget every product's build
    in the same shell at once.

    Nothing in this repository changes when the override is used, so a merged branch cannot
    accidentally keep it switched on - CI never sets the variable and always builds against the
    published package.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <AgoFaqDevOverride Condition="'$(AgoFaqDevOverride)' == ''">false</AgoFaqDevOverride>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
